draftpaper (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The draftpaper command is Rust (cli/), no longer Python: the same
    commands and the same files, written byte for byte as before, and
    fast (the shell's readings every 5 s: 4 ms instead of 116; a click in
    the settings: 9 ms instead of 92). The package no longer needs python3.
  * Settings: one terminal row of mid tones (charcoal, graphite, slate,
    petrol, moss, olive, umber, wine, plum, or as the windows), in place
    of near-black tints and a separate terminal shade; the settings take a
    click at once and redraw only what changed.
  * wlr-output-management: kanshi, wlr-randr and wdisplays change the
    displays' modes, positions, scales and transforms, and turn them off and
    on; displays are named with the make, model and serial from their EDID
    (#30).
  * A screen's zones follow a change of its scale at once.
  * [layout] new_window: a third window opens a new column (as before) or a
    row under the focused window (#12).
  * Touchscreens: a finger goes to the surface under it (wl_touch), and
    a tap focuses the window as a click does; the touch follows the
    laptop panel's rotation.
  * A window of one fixed size (swappy's) floats, centred at its size,
    rather than leaving empty paper in a tile.
  * Window rules ([[rule]] in config.toml): match a window's app id or
    title (patterns) or a browser's picture-in-picture, and float it, keep
    it on every workspace (sticky), place it centred or in the corner, or
    open it without the focus. Built in: picture-in-picture (Meet's, a
    video's) floats in the bottom-right corner, sticky, leaving the focus.
  * A window whose maximum size is below its tile floats rather than
    leaving paper around it.
  * A floating window's border shows over the windows under it (it was
    drawn behind every window, so only tiles, bordered in the gutters,
    showed theirs).
  * Settings on the board (Mod+t, draftpaper settings; it replaces the
    theme picker): the inside of the frame cleared to the sheet's paper
    (with a wallpaper, the picture blurred), the themes as drawings with
    their contrasts, and a colour scheme built from nine choices whose
    lightnesses are solved so that every word reads at 4.5:1 or more
    (#36); a built scheme is kept in [scheme] and the theme "custom".
  * draftpaper theme check: themes against the contrast rules, run by
    make check on the shipped ones. Soft Glow's sheet ink darkened to
    6.6:1, Day Panel's terminal red lightened to 4.5:1.
  * Mod+Ctrl+h/j/k/l resize, as the arrows do.
  * A cheatsheet: every key, click, command and file on one page
    (/usr/share/doc/draftpaper/cheatsheet.md).
  * draftpaper-as USER [COMMAND]: a program, or a shell, as another user on
    the session, for work kept under a separate account.
  * draftpaper-as starts that user's service manager when it is not
    running: started from the desktop, sudo makes no login, and a program
    with no runtime directory has no D-Bus, portal or keyring.

 -- 0x64616e6e <daniel@este.systems>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:15:13 +0300

draftpaper (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Draftpaper is now a Wayland compositor of its own (Smithay), started as
    the "Draftpaper" session from the display manager; the i3 edition is
    dropped (#31).
  * The sheet's margins, title block, side cells and notifications are drawn
    by the shell over the compositor's IPC; merged cells, Nerd Font glyphs.
  * Parking in the side margins, animated; focus follows the mouse.
  * A wallpaper in the frame, with the paper's or the picture's colours in the
    margins.
  * Screenshots, wlr-screencopy (grim, slurp) and screen sharing through
    xdg-desktop-portal-wlr; data control (clipboard managers); fractional
    scaling; linux-dmabuf; Xwayland.
  * Locking (ext-session-lock: swaylock), idle (swayidle): the screens off
    after 15 minutes, locking before sleep on request.
  * Volume and brightness keys; the volume is kept from one session to the
    next.
  * A theme picker (Super+T) with a live preview; a theme also colours
    alacritty, foot, tmux, Neovim, Emacs, GTK 3 and 4, Qt and Firefox (#35).

 -- 0x64616e6e <daniel@este.systems>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 02:53:59 +0300

draftpaper (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Redraw the sheet when screens are added, removed or change mode (#4).
  * Keep parked windows in step with i3: a parked window that closes, changes
    its title or leaves the scratchpad by hand updates its cell (#5).
  * Several custom cells: the first in the title block, the others in the
    bottom margin's free zones (#6).
  * Blueprint, a dark theme; themes gain a "strong" colour for the focused
    workspace (#7).
  * Super+Left/Right cycling moves to its own include, draftpaper-cycle.conf,
    so the main include no longer clashes with i3's focus keys (#8).
  * IBM Plex Mono is recommended (it is in contrib); DejaVu Sans Mono is used
    without it.

